        {
          "id": "simonwillison:https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/12/deepseek-v4-pro-0813",
          "title": "DeepSeek V4 Pro 0813 (on OpenRouter)",
          "url": "https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/12/deepseek-v4-pro-0813",
          "source": "simonwillison",
          "publishedAt": "2026-08-12T23:59:23.000Z",
          "summary": "DeepSeek V4 Pro 0813 (on OpenRouter) The latest DeepSeek Pro model is now available, via API only. I had to link to OpenRouter because DeepSeek don't have any obvious announcement page for their new model. I haven't been able to confirm if they plan to release the open weights, but given the weights are available for both April's deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro and July's deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731 it seems likely. Interestingly I got very different looking pelicans for the three different reasoning levels of low, medium, and high. I've not noticed this kind of difference from any other model: Low: Medium: High: In terms of benchmarks... as far as I can tell those were released to the Official DeepSeek WeChat Group, then copied and pasted into a post on Reddit which was deleted by the moderators for being \"low-effort\", then copied into this ASCII-art table on Hacker News . Tags: ai , generative-ai , llms , pelican-riding-a-bicycle , deepseek , llm-release , ai-in-china",
          "trust": 0.7,
          "signals": { }
        }
